@startuml
title Generic Information Model — Working Concept

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12

rectangle "THING" as Thing
rectangle "STATEMENT" as Statement
rectangle "OBSERVATION" as Observation
rectangle "INTENTION" as Intention
rectangle "RELATIONSHIP" as Relationship
rectangle "CONTEXT" as Context
rectangle "TRANSITION" as Transition
rectangle "MISSION" as Mission

Thing --> Statement : described by
Statement --> Context : interpreted within

Observation --> Statement : observes
Intention --> Statement : expresses desired state / change

Relationship --> Thing : connects
Transition --> Thing : changes / involves
Mission --> Transition : may induce

note right of Thing
  Something the system can refer to.

  Examples:
  person, organisation, business,
  place, event, community, resource.

  No fixed universal taxonomy
  is assumed.
end note

note right of Statement
  Meaningful information about
  a Thing or relationship.

  Example:

  Student
    seeks
  software experience
end note

note right of Observation
  An observation at a point in
  time and context.

  May include source,
  confidence and other
  provenance information.
end note

note right of Intention
  Desired direction, future state,
  outcome or change.

  May be explicit, partial,
  uncertain or emerging.
end note

note right of Context
  Time, place, situation,
  perspective, domain, source
  or other conditions.

  Context gives information
  meaning.
end note

note right of Transition
  Meaningful change from one
  configuration to another.

  May involve one or many
  Things simultaneously.

  A decision may itself be
  a meaningful Transition.
end note

note bottom of Statement
  Identity is a contextual
  projection of relevant
  information about a Thing.

  A "Brick" is a relevant
  aspect of Identity, not
  necessarily a universal type.
end note

note bottom of Transition
  Higher-level concepts such as
  Identity, Opportunity, Goal,
  Vision, Obstacle and Constraint
  are currently treated as
  interpretations or projections
  rather than mandatory primitives.
end note

@enduml
